{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And you shall say.</b> וְגַלְמוּדָה (forsaken), dwelling alone; and like it יְהִי גַלְמוּד (Job 3:7). The root of the word is four letters, and it is an adjective." "<b>Removed.</b> An adjective: she removed from her place. It cannot be a פָּעוֹל form, for סוּר is not among the transitive verbs." "<b>And these, where are they?</b> Two words, with the same sense as אֵיוּ (where are they?)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:48.898622699Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}